* Pointers to structs

Struct fields can be accessed through a struct pointer.

To access the field ⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000001⟫X⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000002⟫ of a struct when we have the struct pointer ⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000003⟫p⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000004⟫ we could
write ⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000005⟫(*p).X⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000006⟫.
However, that notation is cumbersome, so the language permits us instead to
write just ⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000007⟫p.X⟪GTI18N_29695d33_000008⟫, without the explicit dereference.

